From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chromium-blink-ios <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iOS Blink input: guard multi-touch cancellation and stale touches against SIGTRAP

RenderWidgetUIView previously forwarded touchesCancelled:withEvent: one UITouch
at a time to WebTouchEventBuilder::Build(kTouchCancel, ...), which appended
remaining touches as kStateStationary and tripped MotionEventWeb's
CHECK(AllTouchPointsHaveState(kStateCancelled)). Duplicate, untracked, or stale
touches from detached views also triggered CHECK/NOTREACHED traps.

Track active touches with weak view ownership inside base::NoDestructor storage,
drain stale touches, clear a view's touches on removeView, and in
WebTouchEventBuilder::BuildTouchEvents lift preceding or partial-cancel touches
as kTouchEnd (kStateReleased) before emitting kTouchCancel only for the sole
remaining cancelled touch.

---
 components/input/web_input_event_builders_ios.h    |   23 ++
 components/input/web_input_event_builders_ios.mm   |  270 ++++++++++++++++++--
 .../render_widget_host_view_ios_uiview.mm          |   72 ++++-
 3 files changed, 316 insertions(+), 49 deletions(-)

